    "background_story": "Aaron was a brilliant composer known for his innovative approach to music. He experimented with unconventional sounds and rhythms, often incorporating elements of mathematics into his work. Aaron became fascinated with the concept of arity, exploring the relationships between musical notes and their corresponding mathematical functions. He developed a unique composition technique, where he would assign specific arities to different instruments, creating intricate patterns and harmonies. His magnum opus, 'Arity in Harmony,' premiered at a prestigious music festival, receiving critical acclaim for its innovative use of mathematical concepts. The piece was hailed as a masterpiece, demonstrating Aaron's ability to merge art and science in a beautiful, symphonic dance.",
